==English==
{{wikidata lexeme|L133}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂welh₁-|id=rule}}
{{back-formation|en|evaluation}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪˈvaljʊeɪt/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɪˈvæl.juˌeɪt/|/ɪˈvæl.jəˌeɪt/|a=GenAm,CA}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-evaluate.ogg|a=Maryland|IPA=/ɪˈvæl.juˌeɪt/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|eval|u|ate}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪt|s=4}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To draw conclusions from [[examine|examining]]; to [[assess]]; to appraise.
#: {{syn|en|assess|esteem|rate|Thesaurus:appraise}}
#: {{ux|en|It will take several years to '''evaluate''' the material gathered in the survey.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=On Grief and Grieving|author=Elisabeth Kübler-Ross; David Kessler|year=2005|ISBN=9781476775555|page=151
|passage=Death is a factor that changes all our views as we are forced to '''evaluate''' our worth and what ultimately matters in life.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|mathematics|computing}} To [[compute]] or determine the value of (an expression).
#: {{ux|en|'''Evaluate''' this integral.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|computing|mathematics}} To [[return]] or have a specific [[value]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Lev Sabinin; Larissa Sbitneva; Ivan Shestakov|title=Non-Associative Algebra and Its Applications|publisher=CRC Press|ISBN=9780824726690|page=201
|passage=Since element (15.1) '''evaluates''' to an element of the center in any alternative algebra, (15.1) has to '''evaluate''' to a scalar multiple of the identity element of the Cayley-Dickson algebra.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=James E. Gentle|title=Matrix Algebra: Theory, Computations, and Applications in Statistics|publisher=Springer Science & Business Media|ISBN=9780387708720|page=165
|passage=In one type of such an integral, the integrand is only the probability density function, and the integral '''evaluates''' to a probability, which of course is a scalar.}}

